$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Methoxy-5,5,8,8-tetramethyl-6,7-dihydronaphthalene-2-carboxylic acid
(2). Allyl bromide (110 mL, 1.29 mmol, 0.3 equiv.) was added to a
solution of tetralin 3 (1.00 g, 4.3 mmol) in EtOAc (20 mL) and the
solution purged with oxygen gas for several minutes. The mixture was then
irradiated with a 400 W medium pressure mercury lamp under an atmosphere
of oxygen gas. The reaction mixture was intermittently purged with oxygen
gas during the course of the reaction and the progress of the reaction
was monitored by HPLC-MS where the complete conversion through to acid 2
was reached after 48 hours of irradiation. The solvents were then
evaporated and the residue portioned between aqueous NaOH (2M) and Et2O.
The aqueous phase was separated, washed with Et2O, acidified with HCl
(2M) and extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic extracts weredried
(MgSO4) and evaporated. 2 (1.07 g, 4.07 mmol, 95%) as a yellow solid. 1H
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.70 (br, 1H), 8.11 (s, 1H), 6.90 (s, 1H), 4.03 (s,
3H), 1.71-1.61 (m, 4H), 1.29 (s, 6H), 1.27 (s, 6H); LCMS (ES) m/z 263
(MH+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-process simplification, photochemical, medium pressure
mercury lamp (400 W) used, key step, alternatively reaction carried out
with KMnO4 in aqueous NaOH-pyridine decreased yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Concise synthesis of the retinoic acid receptor (RAR) agonist AGN-193836
utilizing a photochemical benzylic oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fish, Paul V.; Ralph, Michael J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Green Chemistry Letters and Reviews (2012), 5(4), 535-538

