$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3. General Procedure for Direct Benzylic
Oxidation of Alkylarenes (1) Using KBr/Oxone® System under Photochemical
Conditions (Method B) (Table 2). To the solution of 1b (37.8 mg, 0.25
mmol) and Oxone® (184.4 mg, 0.30 mmol) in a mixture of CH2Cl2 (1.35 mL)
and H2O (0.15 mL) was added KBr (37.5 mg, 0.30 mmol) at room temperature
and stirred under visible light irradiation for 24 h. Saturated Na2SO3
aqueous solution (10 mL) was added to the reaction mixture and the
product was extracted with AcOEt (15 mL × 3). The combined extracts were
washed by brine (10 mL) and dried over Na2SO4. The organic phase was
concentrated under reduced pressure and the crude product was purified by
silica gel column chromatography (eluent: hexane/AcOEt = 20/1), to give
the desired product 2b. 4-Nitroacetophenone (2b, commercially available)
3-Bromobenzoic acid (2ab, commercially available) Yield 93%. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.37 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.75 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 8.05
(d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 8.26 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 122.6,
128.8, 130.1, 131.1, 133.2, 136.8, 170.6. IR (KBr) 2836, 1688, 1568,
1438, 1311 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, radical mechanism, product depends on amount of oxidant,
amount of KBr, solvent and reaction mechanism, visible light used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct and Selective Benzylic Oxidation of Alkylarenes via C-H
Abstraction Using Alkali Metal Bromides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Moriyama, Katsuhiko; Takemura, Misato; Togo, Hideo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(9), 2414-2417

